## Why This Is Asked
Tests crypto agility, cross-cloud governance, and practical CISSP controls for data at rest and in transit.

## Key Concepts
- Crypto agility and KMS key hierarchies across clouds
- Envelope encryption, per-tenant DEKs, field-level encryption
- Key rotation, revocation, auditability, incident response
- Data residency and edge deployment considerations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo rotation workflow
rotateMasterKey(cloud, keyId) {
  wrapNewDEKWithMasterKey(keyId);
  rewrapAllDataKeys();
  validateNoDowntime();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test key rotation impact on latency and availability?
- What would you monitor to detect key-compromise attempts and how would you respond?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CISSP application to real-world, multi-region auth flows, highlighting threat modeling, token lifecycle, and IR readiness.

## Key Concepts
- STRIDE/PASTA for auth/session threats
- JWT, PKCE, JWKS, token rotation, revocation
- mTLS, RBAC/ABAC in a multi-region service mesh
- IR playbooks and testing strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Token validation sketch
function validateToken(token, jwks) {
  const payload = decode(token);
  if (payload.iss !== expectedIssuer) return false;
  if (payload.exp < Date.now()/1000) return false;
  // signature verify against jwks...
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate revocation in a scalable way?
- What metrics indicate token compromise?
